<!DOCTYPE html>
<html>
<head>
<meta charset="utf-8">
<title>Module 5 Worksheet</title>
<style>
  body {
    font-family: 'Segoe UI', Roboto, Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif;
    color: #1e293b;
    line-height: 1.6;
    margin: 40px auto;
    max-width: 800px;
    padding: 0 20px;
    background-color: #ffffff;
  }
  h1 {
    font-size: 26px;
    color: #0f172a;
    border-bottom: 3px solid #7b4fce;
    padding-bottom: 12px;
    margin-bottom: 24px;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.02em;
  }
  h2, h3 {
    font-size: 18px;
    color: #7b4fce;
    margin-top: 35px;
    margin-bottom: 15px;
    border-left: 4px solid #00c8ff;
    padding-left: 12px;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.05em;
  }
  p {
    font-size: 14px;
    margin-bottom: 12px;
    color: #334155;
  }
  ul {
    list-style-type: none;
    padding-left: 5px;
    margin-bottom: 18px;
  }
  li {
    font-size: 14px;
    margin-bottom: 8px;
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
  }
  .checkbox {
    font-size: 18px;
    font-family: monospace;
    color: #94a3b8;
    margin-right: 10px;
    user-select: none;
  }
  .instructions {
    background-color: #f8fafc;
    border-left: 4px solid #7b4fce;
    padding: 15px;
    margin-bottom: 30px;
    font-size: 13px;
    color: #475569;
    font-style: italic;
  }
  .question {
    font-size: 14px;
    font-weight: bold;
    color: #0f172a;
    margin-top: 25px;
    margin-bottom: 8px;
  }
  .response-box {
    background-color: #f8fafc;
    border: 1px dashed #7b4fce;
    border-left: 4px solid #7b4fce;
    padding: 15px 20px;
    margin: 10px 0 25px 0;
    border-radius: 4px;
    color: #475569;
  }
  .response-label {
    margin: 0 0 6px 0;
    font-size: 10px;
    font-weight: bold;
    color: #7b4fce;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.08em;
    font-family: monospace;
  }
  .response-placeholder {
    margin: 0;
    font-size: 13px;
    color: #94a3b8;
    font-style: italic;
  }
  hr {
    border: 0;
    border-top: 1px solid #e2e8f0;
    margin: 40px 0;
  }
</style>
</head>
<body>
<h1>PlayIQ Module 5 Worksheet: Simplification and Practice</h1>
<div class="instructions"><strong>Instructions:</strong> Complete this worksheet thoughtfully. Remember, PlayIQ is about using AI as a coach, not a crutch. Your goal is to become an independent learner!</div>
<hr>
<h3>Part 1: The 3-Ways Rule</h3>
<div class="question">1. (Short Response) The 3-Ways Rule says a strong learner can explain one idea in more than one way. Why is it dangerous to only know one single definition for a concept?</div>
<div class="response-box">
  <p class="response-label">✍️ Student Response Area (Double-click to type)</p>
  <p class="response-placeholder">[ Type your conceptual answer or explanation here... ]</p>
</div>
<div class="response-box">
  <p class="response-label">✍️ Student Response Area (Double-click to type)</p>
  <p class="response-placeholder">[ Type your conceptual answer or explanation here... ]</p>
</div>
<div class="question">2. (Multiple Choice) Which of the following is NOT one of the typical "3 ways" you can ask an AI to explain a topic?</div>
<ul>
<li><span class="checkbox">&#9744;</span> An analogy</li>
<li><span class="checkbox">&#9744;</span> A step-by-step process</li>
<li><span class="checkbox">&#9744;</span> A 10-page academic essay</li>
<li><span class="checkbox">&#9744;</span> An example-first explanation</li>
</ul>
<div class="question">3. (Scenario) You are struggling to understand how a computer processor works. You ask the AI for an *analogy*. The AI says, "It's like a chef in a kitchen taking orders and cooking." Did this explanation style help? Why or why not?</div>
<div class="response-box">
  <p class="response-label">✍️ Student Response Area (Double-click to type)</p>
  <p class="response-placeholder">[ Type your conceptual answer or explanation here... ]</p>
</div>
<div class="response-box">
  <p class="response-label">✍️ Student Response Area (Double-click to type)</p>
  <p class="response-placeholder">[ Type your conceptual answer or explanation here... ]</p>
</div>
<div class="question">4. (Prompt Improvement) Write a prompt asking your AI Learning Coach to teach you about "Fractions" in three different ways: an analogy, a step-by-step process, and an example-first approach.</div>
<div class="response-box">
  <p class="response-label">✍️ Student Response Area (Double-click to type)</p>
  <p class="response-placeholder">[ Type your conceptual answer or explanation here... ]</p>
</div>
<div class="response-box">
  <p class="response-label">✍️ Student Response Area (Double-click to type)</p>
  <p class="response-placeholder">[ Type your conceptual answer or explanation here... ]</p>
</div>
<div class="question">5. (Teach-Back) Explain a single concept from school (like gravity, or democracy) in two different ways: first as an analogy, and then as a real-world example.</div>
<div class="response-box">
  <p class="response-label">✍️ Student Response Area (Double-click to type)</p>
  <p class="response-placeholder">[ Type your conceptual answer or explanation here... ]</p>
</div>
<div class="response-box">
  <p class="response-label">✍️ Student Response Area (Double-click to type)</p>
  <p class="response-placeholder">[ Type your conceptual answer or explanation here... ]</p>
</div>
<hr>
<h3>Part 2: Safe Simplification</h3>
<div class="question">6. (Short Response) A simple explanation is only useful if it stays accurate. What is the danger of "oversimplifying" a topic?</div>
<div class="response-box">
  <p class="response-label">✍️ Student Response Area (Double-click to type)</p>
  <p class="response-placeholder">[ Type your conceptual answer or explanation here... ]</p>
</div>
<div class="response-box">
  <p class="response-label">✍️ Student Response Area (Double-click to type)</p>
  <p class="response-placeholder">[ Type your conceptual answer or explanation here... ]</p>
</div>
<div class="question">7. (Multiple Choice) What does "bad compression" do to an idea?</div>
<ul>
<li><span class="checkbox">&#9744;</span> It makes the idea sound easy, but it becomes wrong or misses the point.</li>
<li><span class="checkbox">&#9744;</span> It makes the idea clear and still true.</li>
<li><span class="checkbox">&#9744;</span> It makes the idea impossible to read.</li>
<li><span class="checkbox">&#9744;</span> It turns the idea into a 3-Ways Rule.</li>
</ul>
<div class="question">8. (Classification) You ask AI to explain the American Revolution.</div>
<p>Version A: "People got mad about taxes and fought."</p>
<p>Version B: "The American colonies wanted independence from British rule, partly due to unfair taxes without representation in government, leading to a war."</p>
<p>Which is a "too-simple" version that leaves out important details, and which is a "better simple" version?</p>
<div class="response-box">
  <p class="response-label">✍️ Student Response Area (Double-click to type)</p>
  <p class="response-placeholder">[ Type your conceptual answer or explanation here... ]</p>
</div>
<div class="response-box">
  <p class="response-label">✍️ Student Response Area (Double-click to type)</p>
  <p class="response-placeholder">[ Type your conceptual answer or explanation here... ]</p>
</div>
<div class="question">9. (Scenario) You are simplifying a difficult physics concept. You ask the AI for a "better simple" version, but you also ask for a "warning about what students often oversimplify." Why is that warning important?</div>
<div class="response-box">
  <p class="response-label">✍️ Student Response Area (Double-click to type)</p>
  <p class="response-placeholder">[ Type your conceptual answer or explanation here... ]</p>
</div>
<div class="response-box">
  <p class="response-label">✍️ Student Response Area (Double-click to type)</p>
  <p class="response-placeholder">[ Type your conceptual answer or explanation here... ]</p>
</div>
<div class="question">10. (Teach-Back) Explain the difference between simplifying something so it is clear, versus oversimplifying it so it becomes wrong.</div>
<div class="response-box">
  <p class="response-label">✍️ Student Response Area (Double-click to type)</p>
  <p class="response-placeholder">[ Type your conceptual answer or explanation here... ]</p>
</div>
<div class="response-box">
  <p class="response-label">✍️ Student Response Area (Double-click to type)</p>
  <p class="response-placeholder">[ Type your conceptual answer or explanation here... ]</p>
</div>
<hr>
<h3>Part 3: Build a 1-Page Understanding Card</h3>
<div class="question">11. (Short Response) What is a 1-Page Understanding Card, and why is it better than a giant 5-page sheet of copied notes?</div>
<div class="response-box">
  <p class="response-label">✍️ Student Response Area (Double-click to type)</p>
  <p class="response-placeholder">[ Type your conceptual answer or explanation here... ]</p>
</div>
<div class="response-box">
  <p class="response-label">✍️ Student Response Area (Double-click to type)</p>
  <p class="response-placeholder">[ Type your conceptual answer or explanation here... ]</p>
</div>
<div class="question">12. (Multiple Choice) Which of the following should NOT be on a 1-Page Understanding Card?</div>
<ul>
<li><span class="checkbox">&#9744;</span> The core idea</li>
<li><span class="checkbox">&#9744;</span> A simple analogy</li>
<li><span class="checkbox">&#9744;</span> Three paragraphs copied directly from Wikipedia</li>
<li><span class="checkbox">&#9744;</span> Common mistakes to avoid</li>
</ul>
<div class="question">13. (Prompt Improvement) You want to build a 1-Page card for a science test. You write: "Make a study guide for me." Rewrite this prompt so the AI acts as a coach, forcing you to provide your own answers for each section before the AI improves it.</div>
<div class="response-box">
  <p class="response-label">✍️ Student Response Area (Double-click to type)</p>
  <p class="response-placeholder">[ Type your conceptual answer or explanation here... ]</p>
</div>
<div class="response-box">
  <p class="response-label">✍️ Student Response Area (Double-click to type)</p>
  <p class="response-placeholder">[ Type your conceptual answer or explanation here... ]</p>
</div>
<div class="question">14. (Scenario) On your Understanding Card for "Multiplying Decimals," you include a section for "Common Mistake." What is an example of a common mistake you might put there?</div>
<div class="response-box">
  <p class="response-label">✍️ Student Response Area (Double-click to type)</p>
  <p class="response-placeholder">[ Type your conceptual answer or explanation here... ]</p>
</div>
<div class="response-box">
  <p class="response-label">✍️ Student Response Area (Double-click to type)</p>
  <p class="response-placeholder">[ Type your conceptual answer or explanation here... ]</p>
</div>
<div class="question">15. (Teach-Back) Explain how having a 1-Page Understanding Card helps you review faster right before a quiz.</div>
<div class="response-box">
  <p class="response-label">✍️ Student Response Area (Double-click to type)</p>
  <p class="response-placeholder">[ Type your conceptual answer or explanation here... ]</p>
</div>
<div class="response-box">
  <p class="response-label">✍️ Student Response Area (Double-click to type)</p>
  <p class="response-placeholder">[ Type your conceptual answer or explanation here... ]</p>
</div>
<hr>
<h3>Part 4: Practice Without Spoon-Feeding</h3>
<div class="question">16. (Short Response) "Practice is where understanding becomes skill." Why does practice fail if the AI gives away the answer too fast?</div>
<div class="response-box">
  <p class="response-label">✍️ Student Response Area (Double-click to type)</p>
  <p class="response-placeholder">[ Type your conceptual answer or explanation here... ]</p>
</div>
<div class="response-box">
  <p class="response-label">✍️ Student Response Area (Double-click to type)</p>
  <p class="response-placeholder">[ Type your conceptual answer or explanation here... ]</p>
</div>
<div class="question">17. (Multiple Choice) When you are practicing math problems with AI, what should you ask for if you get stuck?</div>
<ul>
<li><span class="checkbox">&#9744;</span> The final answer immediately.</li>
<li><span class="checkbox">&#9744;</span> A completely different problem.</li>
<li><span class="checkbox">&#9744;</span> A hint instead of the solution.</li>
<li><span class="checkbox">&#9744;</span> A 1-Page Understanding Card.</li>
</ul>
<div class="question">18. (Scenario) You are practicing Spanish vocabulary. The AI asks you a question, and you don't know it. Instead of asking for the answer, you ask, "Can you give me the first letter and tell me if it sounds like an English word?" Is this a good way to practice without spoon-feeding? Why?</div>
<div class="response-box">
  <p class="response-label">✍️ Student Response Area (Double-click to type)</p>
  <p class="response-placeholder">[ Type your conceptual answer or explanation here... ]</p>
</div>
<div class="response-box">
  <p class="response-label">✍️ Student Response Area (Double-click to type)</p>
  <p class="response-placeholder">[ Type your conceptual answer or explanation here... ]</p>
</div>
<div class="question">19. (Reflection) Think of a skill you are good at (like a sport, a video game, or playing an instrument). Did you get good at it by having someone do it for you, or by practicing and failing? How does this apply to using AI for schoolwork?</div>
<div class="response-box">
